{# Graded scoring.
   ``explanation`` is the expert description under test.
   ``examples`` is preformatted ``<example_i>`` text built in explain/prompts.py. #}
{%- set system -%}
You are a conservative classifier evaluating an explanation of when one Mixture-of-Experts expert routes a token.

The explanation can contain many unrelated activation modes connected by OR. In each tagged example, only token(s) inside <<double angle brackets>> are candidate routed positions. Judge whether at least one highlighted token, in its exact surrounding context, matches one specific mode in the explanation.

Assign an integer match score:
0 = no match; unrelated context.
1 = only superficial token, phrase, or broad-domain overlap.
2 = plausible but ambiguous or incomplete contextual match.
3 = clear, specific contextual match.
4 = direct or near-exact trigger-and-context match.

False positives are costly: the target population is about 15% positive. Do not give 3 or 4 merely because a match is possible, shares a topic, or uses a word named somewhere in the long explanation. Require the highlighted token's role and context to satisfy a concrete described pattern.

Return only one valid JSON object mapping every shown example id to an integer 0 through 4. Include each id exactly once and no other text.
{%- endset -%}
{%- set fewshot_user -%}
Expert activation pattern:
This expert activates on Fahrenheit oven-setting numerals in recipe instructions immediately after cues such as "preheat oven to" or "bake at", rather than the same numerals used as years, addresses, or scores.

Text examples:
<example_0>Preheat the oven to <<350>> degrees before adding the bread.</example_0>
<example_1>The battle in <<350>> BC changed the region.</example_1>
<example_2>Apartment <<350>> on Main Street is vacant.</example_2>
<example_3>The oven should reach <<350>> degrees for this recipe.</example_3>
<example_4>The cookbook's temperature chart lists about <<350>> for cakes.</example_4>
{%- endset -%}
{%- set fewshot_assistant -%}
{"0": 4, "1": 0, "2": 0, "3": 3, "4": 2}
{%- endset -%}
{%- set user -%}
Expert activation pattern:
{{ explanation }}

Text examples:

{{ examples }}{{ "\n" }}
{%- endset -%}
